  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened capacities of tripartite constituents to facilitate the transition of economic units in the informal economy to formality</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since 2021, the economy has been on a positive growth trajectory with real GDP growth of 8.5% in 2021, 6.5% in 2022, estimate of 5,5% in 2023 and a projected growth rate of 3,5% in 2024. The decline in 2024 is attributed to the anticipated Elnino drought which affect mostly the agriculture sector. The 2019 LFCLS estimated an unemployment rate of 16 per cent in 2019 while the 2014 Labour Force and Child Labour Survey (LFCLS) estimated active unemployment at 11.3 percent. whereas in 2023 the unemployment rate was 20.7 based on LFS .. Informal employment, which stood at 94.5 per cent in 2014, declined to an estimated 75.6% according to the 2019 LFCLS and increasing again to 86.8% in 2023. Informality remains a serious obstacle for Decent Work for all. Cross-cutting Policy Drivers Social dialogue will be a key strategy for the delivery of the results in this CPO, which will allow for an effective consultative process ensuring the participation of key stakeholders within government, employers, workers and civil society organizations. Zimbabwe has a tripartite OSH Council (ZOSHC) which is functional, and the OSH Division (at NSSA) serves as secretariat thereto. NSSA administer 4 statutes (Factory and Work Act, Pneumoconiosis Act, Accident Prevention &amp; Workman Compensation Act and NSSA Act) and 8 regulations. The process has commenced to harmonize these laws, with possibility of removing the exclusion government employees from the provisions of the Accident Prevention &amp; Workman Compensation Act.</narrative>
  </description>
